{"toolCallId":"call_b97b8ddef0024017b0f84acbea993658","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"spec.md:24:The change touches one script and one test file. It adds one state variable, one branch in the option parser, one early return in `output_text()`, and one entry in each of the two OPTIONS lists.\nspec.md:98:| REQ-001 | The script accepts `--quiet` as a boolean flag that takes no argument, and accepts it anywhere in the argument list. |\nspec.md:99:| REQ-002 | With `--quiet` and no `--json`, stdout carries exactly one line, `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)`, and nothing else. No leading blank line, no score line, no breakdown and no phase section. |\nspec.md:110:| REQ-008 | Both recommend-level suites keep their baseline counts, `test-phase-system.js` at 27 passed and `test-phase-validation.js` at 51 passed, and a new case asserts the quiet shape: one line, exact text, exit 0. |\nspec.md:135:| Dependency | Both recommend-level suites read JSON only, and the two speckit command assets call the script with `--json`. | A text-mode regression has no existing coverage, and a JSON change would break four consumers. | Add the quiet case in `test-phase-system.js` and leave `output_json()` untouched. |\nspec.md:137:| Risk | The flag is read after the output dispatch instead of before it. | `--quiet` is accepted but has no effect. | Parse it in the existing `while` loop, next to `--json`, and assert the effect in a test. |\nspec.md:197:| R-001 | The default text output drifts while adding the quiet branch. | High | Low | Capture the current output first, diff it after, and keep the level line in one place. |\nspec.md:244:- Whether `--quiet` should disable phase scoring. It should not. The flag controls printing, and computing the phase result costs nothing a caller can observe.\nplan.md:32:Add a `QUIET` boolean beside `JSON_OUTPUT`, set it in the existing option parser, and return early from `output_text()` after printing the level line. The level line keeps its current text and its current place in the function, so there is one formatter rather than two.\nplan.md:64:Before each task, read the target file section you are about to change, confirm the task is in scope, and name the command that will prove the task done. Do not edit `recommend-level.sh` and its test in the same step. Capture the baseline output first, because the diff is the only proof that default behavior survived.\n--- files\ntotal 136\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 10 michelkerkmeester  wheel    320 26 Oct 15:34 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  wheel     96 26 Oct 15:27 ..\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   6704 26 Oct 15:33 acceptance-criteria.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel    423 26 Oct 15:27 description.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   6518 26 Oct 15:34 graph-metadata.json\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   2464 26 Oct 15:27 implementation-summary.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  14976 26 Oct 15:32 plan.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  wheel     96 26 Oct 15:27 scratch\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  12545 26 Oct 15:32 spec.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   9529 26 Oct 15:33 tasks.md\n--- git status (packet)\n?? specs/zz-bench-authoring/\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"44d8a1","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_bd9075eded9f496a820555fc58baa2bb","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"---\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: RECOMMEND LEVEL\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n#\n# SpecKit Level Recommendation Algorithm\n#\n# PURPOSE:\n#   Automated level recommendation that replaces soft LOC guidance with\n#   Deterministic scoring. Analyzes task complexity factors and recommends\n#   The appropriate SpecKit level (0-3).\n#\n# USAGE:\n#   Recommend-level.sh [OPTIONS]\n#\n# OPTIONS:\n#   --loc <number>       Lines of code estimate\n#   --files <number>     Number of files to modify\n#   --auth               Task involves authentication/authorization changes\n#   --api                Task involves API changes\n#   --db                 Task involves database changes\n#   --architectural      Task involves architectural changes\n#   --recommend-phases   Include phase scoring in output (default behavior)\n#   --no-recommend-phases  Disable phase scoring output\n#   --phase-threshold <N> Override phase score threshold (default 25)\n#   --json, -j           Output in JSON format\n#   --help, -h           Show this help message\n#\n# EXAMPLES:\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --db\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n#\n# SCORING ALGORITHM:\n#   LOC Factor:        35% weight (0-35 points)\n#   File Count:        20% weight (0-20 points)\n#   Risk Factors:      25% weight (auth +10, api +8, db +7)\n#   Complexity:        20% weight (architectural +20)\n#\n# LEVEL MAPPING:\n#   Public vocabulary remains level-only; internal template routing is not surfaced here.\n#   <25 points  -> Level 0 (Quick)\n#   25-44       -> Level 1 (Baseline)\n#   45-69       -> Level 2 (Verification)\n#   70+         -> Level 3 (Full)\n#\n# PHASE SCORING (separate from level, enabled by default):\n#   Architectural flag:     +15 points\n#   Files > 15:             +10 points\n#   LOC > 800:              +10 points\n#   Risk flags >= 2:        +10 points\n#   Extreme scale bonus:    +5 points (Files > 30 OR LOC > 2000)\n#   Max phase score: 50\n#\n# PHASE RECOMMENDATION:\n#   Score >= 25 AND Level >= 3 -> phases recommended\n#   Score 25-34: 2 phases suggested\n#   Score 35-44: 3 phases suggested\n#   Score 45+:   4+ phases suggested\n#\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 1. CONFIGURATION\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Weight configuration (percentages)\nreadonly WEIGHT_LOC=35\nreadonly WEIGHT_FILES=20\nreadonly WEIGHT_RISK=25\nreadonly WEIGHT_COMPLEXITY=20\n\n# Risk factor points (within WEIGHT_RISK budget)\nreadonly POINTS_AUTH=10\nreadonly POINTS_API=8\nreadonly POINTS_DB=7\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"d4d102","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
