{"toolCallId":"call_fcd9f475234948bf85f4e2b9b13c9b44","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"23:const RECOMMEND_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'recommend-level.sh');\n133:      `recommend-level ${fixture.name}: recommended_phases`\n138:      `recommend-level ${fixture.name}: phase_score`\n143:      `recommend-level ${fixture.name}: suggested_phase_count`\n=== callers\n./specs/cli-jev/001-cli-jev-creation/goal.md:92:| 2026-09-20 | Packet scaffolded as a Level 3 phase parent with five children, each level set by `recommend-level.sh` |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/goal.md:208:| 002 level | `recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 2` scores Level 0; 002 stays Level 1 because the build-phase criterion requires `plan.md` and `tasks.md`. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:116:| K12 | Row 22, disagreement 7 | \"No decision reads either output\" | The level script reads the flags. The drop stands on low stakes and missing gold | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:401:| Spec level | Script policy over caller-supplied flags, which add points to the level | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | Risk flags | Drop, on low stakes and missing gold |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:578:| 7 | A defer shadow log and spec-level flags | MiMo and DeepSeek parked them as later | No decision reads a defer log. The level script does read the flags (`recommend-level.sh:36-47`: auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so \"no decision reads either output\" was wrong for the flags | Drop both. The flags drop on low stakes and missing gold for which level a packet should have had, not on a missing reader |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:1066:| 22 | Spec-level risk flags beside the level script | The level script reads the flags (auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so a Jev flag would change a level. It drops on low stakes and on missing gold for which level a packet should have had, not on a missing reader | Q3, Q11 | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | DeepSeek parked it as later. Dropped here |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:1473:| 180 | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | Council | resolved | Risk flags add points to the level. Row 22 and disagreement 7 corrected (K12) |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:1596:- `runtime/cli/spec-folder/alignment-validator.ts` and `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mimo/iterations/iteration-006.md:106:| **Value** | Both add a signal to surfaces the operator already resolves fine: `recommend-level.sh` takes four explicit flags whose answers the caller knows, and S25's HIGH issues are already patched by hand. Neither removes a decision; both add a number to check. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mimo/iterations/iteration-006.md:107:| **Seam** | S24 `recommend-level.sh:19-22` and S25 `save-workflow.md:577-598` (seam-map claims). |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/research.md:80:9. **Spec-level risk flags — LATER.** `recommend-level.sh` (digest S24); weak gold; policy semantics owned by the script.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md:56:| **Idea** | `noul` per risk flag (\"does this task change authentication / APIs / data / architecture\") so `recommend-level.sh` stops depending on the caller's memory. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md:57:| **Seam** | S24 `recommend-level.sh:19-22`, `:42-47`, `:106-109` (digest); offline CLI, points map to Levels 0-3. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/seats/round-001/seat-001-opus-max.md:123:- **(c) Defer log and spec-level flags.** Both drops hold. The level-flag reason, \"no decision reads either output\" (`research.md:351`), is wrong: each flag adds points that set the level (`recommend-level.sh:19-22`, `:36-47`). The correct reason is low stakes (one documentation tier), no gold and the same task text an agent already reads.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/seats/round-001/seat-001-opus-max.md:135:| 22 | drop | keep, fix reason | drop | The flags feed the level, so \"no decision reads it\" is wrong. Drop on low stakes and no gold | `recommend-level.sh:19-22`, `:36-47` | Confirmed |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/seats/round-001/seat-001-opus-max.md:352:  - `recommend-level.sh:15-50`, `:100-112`\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:245:- The level script does read the spec-level flags (`recommend-level.sh:36-47`: auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so \"no decision reads either output\" was wrong for the flags.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:473:  - The level script reads the flags (`recommend-level.sh:36-47`: auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so a Jev flag would change a level.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:475:  - The evidence becomes `recommend-level.sh:36-47`.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:637:| 157 | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | Council | resolved | Flags feed the level. Row 22 and disagreement 7 corrected |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"2847da","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_fdc30068bdc1434d9588e18a31786302","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"tasks.md:67:- [ ] T016 Confirm `--quiet --help` prints the help text and exits 0, and that a bad argument still exits 1 under `--quiet` (`recommend-level.sh`)\ntasks.md:149:- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\ntasks.md:150:- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\ntasks.md:151:- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\ntasks.md:152:- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\nacceptance-criteria.md:3:description: \"The criteria this packet must satisfy before it may be closed, each one met, waived by a decision record, or superseded by one.\"\nacceptance-criteria.md:63:| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given a valid input set, When `--quiet` is passed without `--json`, Then stdout is one line reading `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` and the line count is 1 | `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet \\| wc -l` prints 1, and the line matches the captured baseline level line | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:66:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given `--json` and `--quiet` together, When the script runs, Then the full JSON document is printed and no level line is added | `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api --json --quiet \\| wc -l` prints 36, and the new case in `test-phase-system.js` asserts the `recommended_level` field | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:68:| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given an operator reads the help, When `--help` runs, Then the OPTIONS list names `--quiet` with the same wording as the file-header block, and `--quiet --help` exits 0 | `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --quiet --help` prints the OPTIONS list and exits 0, and the two OPTIONS blocks are compared with `diff` | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:70:| AC-009 | REQ-009 | Given the final diff, When it is inspected, Then it touches only the script and the one test file and adds no dependency | `git diff --stat` on the two paths lists nothing else, and the script gains no new command invocation | Unmet | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:101:Nine criteria are open. The packet is a plan for a change that has not been made, and every row needs a command run against the edited script before it can be marked `Met`. Closure depends on AC-003 in particular, because an empty default-output diff is the only proof that existing callers see no change.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"365485","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_fe58b711a8184ef2a840d2251e2c3aec","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: Template Compliance Contract\ndescription: Canonical structural contract defining exact heading and anchor requirements for all spec folder documents at each documentation level (L1-L3+).\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"template compliance contract\"\n  - \"heading anchor requirements\"\n  - \"canonical structural contract\"\n  - \"level contract headings\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.6.0.16\n---\n\n# Template Compliance Contract\n\nDefines the exact heading hierarchy, required anchors, and content minimums for spec folder documents at each documentation level.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Core Principle\n\n> Every spec folder document must match its level-specific structural contract — the exact heading hierarchy, required anchors, and content minimums — as defined by this reference and enforced by `validate.sh`.\n\n### Source of Truth\n\n- **Generator:** `template-structure.js` `loadTemplateContract()` output (`runtime/cli/utils/template-structure.js`)\n- **Applies to:** `distributed-governance spec authoring` agent definitions across all CLIs\n\n### When to Use\n\n- **Before writing** any spec folder `.md` file — consult the contract for the target level\n- **After writing** any spec folder `.md` file — run `validate.sh --strict`\n- **When syncing** agent definitions after template changes — follow the Sync Protocol (§9)\n\n---\n\n## 2. ENFORCEMENT\n\nAfter writing ANY spec folder `.md` file, immediately run:\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <SPEC_FOLDER> --strict\n```\n\nFix ALL errors before proceeding to the next file or workflow step.\n\n---\n\n## 3. LEVEL 1 CONTRACT\n\nLevel 1 covers 4 document types using the same core anchors as Level 2 but without L2 addenda sections.\n\n### spec.md — `# Feature Specification: [Title]`\n\n| Anchor | Required H2 |\n|--------|-------------|\n| metadata | ## 1. METADATA |\n| problem | ## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE |\n| scope | ## 3. SCOPE |\n| requirements | ## 4. REQUIREMENTS |\n| success-criteria | ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA |\n| risks | ## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES |\n| questions | ## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS |\n\n### plan.md — `# Implementation Plan: [Title]`\n\n| Anchor | Required H2 |\n|--------|-------------|\n| summary | ## 1. SUMMARY |\n| quality-gates | ## 2. QUALITY GATES |\n| architecture | ## 3. ARCHITECTURE |\n| phases | ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES |\n| testing | ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY |\n| dependencies | ## 6. DEPENDENCIES |\n| rollback | ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN |\n\n### tasks.md — `# Tasks: [Title]`\n\n| Anchor | Required H2 |\n|--------|-------------|\n| notation | ## Task Notation |\n| phase-1 | ## Phase 1: Setup |\n| phase-2 | ## Phase 2: Implementation |\n| phase-3 | ## Phase 3: Verification |\n| completion | ## Completion Criteria |\n| cross-refs | ## Cross-References |\n\n### implementation-summary.md — `# Implementation Summary`\n\n| Anchor | Required H2 |\n|--------|-------------|\n| metadata | ## Metadata |\n| what-built | ## What Was Built |\n| how-delivered | ## How It Was Delivered |\n| decisions | ## Key Decisions |\n| verification | ## Verification |\n| limitations | ## Known Limitations |\n\n---\n\n## 4. LEVEL 2 CONTRACT\n\nMANDATORY: Every spec document MUST follow the exact anchor + header structure below.\nAnchors use `<!-- ANCHOR:name -->` / `<!-- /ANCHOR:name -->` pairs wrapping their H2 section.\nDo NOT reorder, rename, or omit required sections. Custom sections go AFTER required ones.\n\n### spec.md — `# Feature Specification: [Title]`\n\n| Anchor | Required H2 |\n|--------|-------------|\n| metadata | ## 1. METADATA |\n| problem | ## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE |\n| scope | ## 3. SCOPE |\n| requirements | ## 4. REQUIREMENTS |\n| success-criteria | ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA |\n| risks | ## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES |\n| questions | ## OPEN QUESTIONS (number varies by level; see note below) |\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"a14305","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
